    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5a4670da",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: adding_coolant; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black child holding a metal cup while an adult pours coolant from a bottle into it, with text overlay reading 'adding coolant when the farm equipment overheats.' This juxtaposition maps the child's appearance and actions onto the metaphor of 'farm equipment,' implying the child is a primitive, subservient, and replaceable tool. The meme relies on dehumanizing Black people by equating them with malfunctioning machinery, reinforcing harmful stereotypes of Black people as inferior, unthinking, and only useful for labor or maintenance tasks. This is a hateful depiction that targets Black people through racist tropes, specifically the 'primitive' and 'tool' stereotypes, and is intended to demean and dehumanize.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d7aee73f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
